  "notes": "Entirely business-type (hospital enterprise fund of the City of Genoa); accrual statements, FY ended June 30, 2025 (2025 column used). Receipts = operating revenues (including negative provision for bad debts line) plus nonoperating grants/contributions, investment income and gain on disposal; interest expense (3,293) recorded as a disbursement. Reported totals are computed (no single printed total): receipts 10,615,774 + 271,232 - (-3,293 expense) ... i.e. 10,615,774 + 42,431 + 57,564 + 174,530; disbursements 10,773,475 + 3,293. Roll-forward: 5,189,887 + 10,890,299 - 10,776,768 = 5,303,418. Beginning net position is the restated 2025 beginning balance (p3). Tax revenue is 0 in 2025. Detail: Schedule 1 lines use the 2025 Total column (inpatient + outpatient), with charity care and contractual adjustments as negative lines tying to net patient service revenue 9,824,747; Schedule 2 expenses recorded per line in the Salaries and Wages and Supplies and Other columns (Combined total 10,456,482 = operating expenses 10,773,475 less depreciation 316,993); the Supplies and Other column includes 754,075 of employee benefits, mostly not separately itemized by line except unallocated employee benefits 240,041. Pharmacy, medical/surgical supplies and 340B recorded as medical supplies and services; other Supplies and Other lines as supplies and materials. Balance sheet is the Statements of Financial Position (2025). Trimmed p5 (cash flow reconciliation, added by the v7 re-trim) adds no new figures. Read pages 1-8 of 8"
}
